@!internal

--[[
Native implementation of [](nupp.runtime.contracts)' UUID provider.

Version 4 is random; version 7 orders by the wall clock's milliseconds, then
random bits. Both draw their bytes from the operating system through
[](nupp.runtime.provider.osentropy), return the canonical lowercase,
hyphenated spelling, and raise if the system cannot supply randomness.

The [](nupp.runtime.uuidprovider) facade retains the selected functions once.
UUID randomness is supplied by the operating system rather than Lua's random
seed, so a restored checkpoint repeats none.
]]
module nupp.runtime.provider.osuuid

const entropy = require("nupp.runtime.provider.osentropy")
const spelling = require("nupp.runtime.uuidspelling")
const clock = require("nupp.vm.clock")

--- Generates a random version 4 UUID.
---
--- @return the UUID, hyphenated and lowercase
--- @raises string when the system has no randomness to draw on
export function uuid4(): string
    return spelling.spell(entropy.randombytes(spelling.RANDOM_BYTES), 4)
end

--- Generates a time-ordered version 7 UUID.
---
--- @return the UUID, hyphenated and lowercase
--- @raises string when the system has no randomness to draw on
export function uuid7(): string
    local milliseconds = math.floor(clock.wallTime()) as integer

    return spelling.spell(entropy.randombytes(spelling.RANDOM_BYTES), 7, milliseconds)
end
